ndShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-21T13:09:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T13:09:15Z","body":"Tested and it works on Linux at least, haven't tested other platforms. My findings is however that it's very slow, as it just uses the standard `addr2line` program, we could look for the gimli and llvm variants like we do for the crash handler on Linux\r\n\r\nBut I'm wondering if this would be better integrated into the engine itself, that would allow us to reuse the same code for doing that lookup and we could change it to allow us to provide the executable to the method and when invoked with a new command like `--retrace` called on the engine itself, and it delegates that, this would make it easier to retrace without having to access the engine source as well","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6316869884/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6317207000","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124394#issuecomment-6317207000","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124394","id":6317207000,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABeIjt2A","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html